{"seq":23,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-mcp-instructions-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:09:48.982Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"dbc23b760bbe265215578e2f37f112057ab9b3a775688c728c1a3ad09b8d8eb5","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Tobias, I found three Marrow Fieldworks ticket numbers:\n\n*From Moss's notes* (teams/team-central/digests/2026-01-02-central-handoffs.md, \"Central handoffs next week\", 2 Jan 2026):\n• *#4409*: a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake). Hollis flagged it as open before the 5 Jan handoff.\n• *#4412*: a driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots. It was also flagged as open before the handoff.\n\n*From #central-random* (your message on 13 Oct, 09:27):\n• *#8841*: West yard Door 2 at the Plains depots is still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk. You flagged this to support while checking the tractor-bay webhook patch.\n\nA few things to know:\n• None of these sources actually says \"#8841 is Marrow Fieldworks.\" The Moss note says Marrow Fieldworks was handed off on 5 Jan and calls it \"Pree's dealer account.\" #central-random calls it \"Tobias's dealer account.\" I've treated them as the same account, but please check that before the call.\n• I left out FR-882 from the same Moss note. That's a feature request from *Marrow Agrisupply*, a different account. I also left out PD-4821 (Marrow Agrisupply, in #central-team).\n• Moss's Central cheat sheet has no ticket numbers for Fieldworks, and I couldn't find an account folder for Marrow Fieldworks. I also can't confirm whether #4409 and #4412 are still open; the note only shows their status as of January."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":24,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-mcp-instructions-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:09:54.371Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"db44dc9b9907b82e1ee46c47a31a00846f0827a7af7c6028bf9ad2dc233adde9","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found three ticket numbers for Marrow Fieldworks and sent you the list in our DM, with where each one comes from:\n\n- **#4409**, from Moss's Central handoffs note (2 Jan 2026). It's a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard, during the 06:00 flatbed intake. Hollis flagged it as open before the 5 Jan handoff.\n- **#4412**, from the same Moss note. It's a driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots. It was also flagged as open before the handoff.\n- **#8841**, from your own message in #central-random (13 Oct, 09:27). West yard Door 2 at the Plains depots is still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk.\n\nBefore the call:\n- **Check #8841 is really Fieldworks.** Nothing names Marrow Fieldworks next to #8841. The Moss note says Fieldworks changed hands on 5 Jan and calls it \"Pree's dealer account.\" #central-random calls it \"Tobias's dealer account.\" I treated them as the same account, but that's my guess.\n- **#4409 and #4412 may be closed by now.** The note only shows them as open in January, and I couldn't confirm their status since.\n- **I left out two numbers that belong to Marrow Agrisupply, a different account.** FR-882 (a feature request in the same Moss note) and PD-4821 (in #central-team).\n- **The other sources had nothing more.** Moss's Central cheat sheet has no Fieldworks ticket numbers, and there's no account folder for Marrow Fieldworks."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
